\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces Rotated path on the inverted Rosen--Morse potential by~$\theta $. The black points and the blue points denote the turning points and the double poles, respectively. The orange path is the usual contour ($\theta =0$) given in~Figs.~\ref {src:2505_02301:fig:stokes_graph_path} and \ref {src:2505_02301:fig:zel_integration}, which is rotated by~$\theta $ under the CSM. The endpoints of the path in the CSM are at~$x=\pm \infty $, and so the interval of the integration $\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ S_{\mathrm  {odd}}$ is smaller than the usual one by~$\theta $. $I'_\infty $ is finite for $0<\theta <\pi /4$.}}{146}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
