\newlabel{src:2510_11766:fig:ho4_energy_pert}{{7.5}{195}{The ground state energy of the anharmonic oscillator as a function of~$g$. This is based on the next-to-leading estimate in the perturbation theory in terms of~$g$. The quantum numbers, $n_r$ and~$l$, are set to vanish, so $\lambda =1/2$ under the Langer correction. Typically, the energy is damping monotonically with respect to the perturbation parameter~$g$}{figure.caption.59}{}}
